{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MonodromyTraceInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.MonodromyTraceInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.det_odd_word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.det_odd_word","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MonodromyTraceInvariance.lean#L82-L86","doc":"And an odd-length word has `det = −1`, so it cannot meet the `det = 1` field\nat all — the braid image splits cleanly by parity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.det_even_word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.det_even_word","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MonodromyTraceInvariance.lean#L74-L80","doc":"Every generator of the braid image has `det = −1` in the `(2,1)` block\n(measured in the probe), so an **even-length** word has `det = +1` exactly. The\ncarrier's `M.det = 1` field is automatic on the braid image — it was never the\nobstruction; the trace field is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.trace_conj_of_mul_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.trace_conj_of_mul_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MonodromyTraceInvariance.lean#L60-L72","doc":"**Conjugation preserves the trace.** Stated with a one-sided inverse so it\nneeds no `Invertible` instance: `Q * P = 1` is all the gauge equivalence\nsupplies, and all the argument uses.\n\nThis is the whole of why branch 3's monodromy reading closes. A connection whose\nmonodromy reproduces the Hecke braiding has holonomies of the form `P * ρ(w) * Q`\nwith `Q * P = 1`; their traces are therefore *exactly* `tr ρ(w)`, which the probe\nmeasures to be Laurent polynomials in `q`. The carrier needs a transcendental\ntrace, so no such monodromy is a carrier. ","signatureChunk":0}]}